## Why This Is Asked

This question tests understanding of augmented binary search trees to support order statistics—a fundamental data structures concept.

## Key Concepts

- **Augmented BST/Treap**: Each node stores value, count (for duplicates), and subtreeSize
- **Order statistics**: getKthSmallest navigates using left subtree size and node counts
- **Duplicate handling**: Multiple identical values stored in a single node with a count field
- **Rebalancing**: Operations maintain O(log n) time via rotations or split/merge

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.c = 1;      // count of this value
    this.sz = 1;     // subtree size
    this.l = null;
    this.r = null;
    this.p = null;  // priority for treap
  }

  upd() {
    this.sz = (this.l?.sz || 0) + (this.r?.sz || 0) + this.c;
  }
}

function kth(node, k) {
  if (!node) return null;
  const leftSize = node.l?.sz || 0;
  if (k <= leftSize) return kth(node.l, k);
  if (k <= leftSize + node.c) return node.v;
  return kth(node.r, k - leftSize - node.c);
}
```

## Time Complexity

- Insert: O(log n)
- EraseOne: O(log n)
- GetKthSmallest: O(log n)

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a simple data structure with guaranteed O(1) operations and handle edge cases like duplicates and emptiness.

## Key Concepts

- Two-stack technique to keep current minimum per depth
- Constant-time top and getMin
- Correct empty-state handling and error signaling

## Code Example

```javascript
class MinStack {
  constructor() {
    this.stack = [];
    this.mins = [];
  }
  push(x) {
    this.stack.push(x);
    if (this.mins.length === 0) {
      this.mins.push(x);
    } else {
      this.mins.push(Math.min(x, this.mins[this.mins.length - 1]));
    }
  }
  pop() {
    if (this.stack.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    this.stack.pop();
    this.mins.pop();
  }
  top() {
    if (this.stack.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.stack[this.stack.length - 1];
  }
  getMin() {
    if (this.mins.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.mins[this.mins.length - 1];
  }
}
```

